# Protocol 01: Environment and Tools

## Purpose

Own installation, capability checks, configuration and prerequisites. It
does not define Design System intent.

### General policy

Before changing tools: check existing installation; use
official/approved sources; prefer project-scoped reproducibility; never
invent commands; record version/scope/verification; never store secrets.
A tool is `READY` only after verification.

### Graphify

Official authority: `https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify`

Current official documentation recommends Python 3.10+ and `uv`.
Preferred install:

``` bash
uv tool install graphifyy
graphify install --project --platform codex
graphify --help
```

The package is `graphifyy`; CLI is `graphify`. Codex uses `$graphify`,
not `/graphify`. Graphify currently documents `multi_agent = true` under
`[features]` in `~/.codex/config.toml` for parallel extraction.

Expected outputs: `graphify-out/graph.html`, `GRAPH_REPORT.md`,
`graph.json`. Prefer scoped graph queries when the graph is current.
Preserve EXTRACTED/INFERRED provenance. Refresh after meaningful
contract, registry, implementation, QA or architecture changes.

### Figma MCP

**Installation source pending the user-provided reference.** Do not
invent installation/configuration.

Before Figma work verify required capabilities: inspect
files/pages/nodes; read variables and component metadata; write required
structures; bind variables; manipulate components/variants when needed;
read results back. Missing required capability =\> `BLOCKED`.

Before writes identify exact Figma file, target page/area, confirm it is
the reconstruction target, and inspect existing content. Never modify
the original source library without explicit authorization.

### Front-end

Planned stack: React, TypeScript, Vite; Storybook when component
isolation begins. Do not install during Figma-only reconstruction unless
required. When web phase starts, record/pin Node, package manager,
framework versions, token pipeline,
lint/test/accessibility/visual-regression tooling and build commands.

Maintain `registry/environment.md` with tool, status, version, scope,
source, verification, last_verified, notes. No secrets.
